# DESCRIPTION

Section 4 describes the file servers.
Every service in the system is a file server: a process that serves a tree of files over 9Px (see intro(5)), posted by name in `/srv`, which a process mounts into its namespace.
A server's page lists its files and what writing to its `ctl` file does.

svcd(8) starts the servers from their manifests and keeps their names in `/srv`, so a client that connects while a server restarts waits for it rather than failing.

